msgid "General program structure"
msgstr "通用程序结构"

msgid ""
"This chapter gives an overview of the most important features of Molpro. For"
" the new user, it is essential to understand the strategies and conventions "
"described in this section, in particular the meaning of *files* and "
"*records*, and the use of *symmetry*. This chapter will focus on general "
"aspects; detailed information about each command will be given in later "
"chapters. Information about commands and parameters can also be obtained "
"using the Molpro help facility (see section `molpro help "
"<general_program_structure.html#molpro-help>`__)."
msgstr ""
"本章概述了 Molpro 最重要的特性。对于新用户来说，理解本节描述的策略和约定至关重要，特别是 *文件* 和 *记录* 的含义，以及 *对称性* "
"的使用。本章将侧重于一般性方面；每个命令的详细信息将在后续章节中给出。有关命令和参数的信息也可以通过 Molpro 帮助工具获取（参见 `molpro "
"help <general_program_structure.html#molpro-help>`__ 节）。"

msgid "Input structure"
msgstr "输入结构"

msgid "A typical ``MOLPRO`` input has the following structure:"
msgstr "一个典型的 ``MOLPRO`` 输入具有以下结构："

msgid "Files"
msgstr "文件"

msgid ""
"Molpro uses three sequential text files, namely the *input file*, the "
"*output file*, and the *punch file*. The punch file is a short form of the "
"output which contains the most important data and results, such as "
"geometries, energies, dipole moments, etc. The punch file can be processed "
"by the separate program *READPUN*, which selects specific results by "
"keywords and is able to produce ordered tables in user supplied format. "
"Furthermore, there are up to 9 binary Molpro files available, each one known"
" to the program simply by its number (1 to 9). By default, they are "
"temporary files, usually allocated dynamically by the program, but they can "
"be connected to permanent files with the ``FILE`` command. Each file is "
"direct access, and word addressable (word=64 bit usually), but is organised "
"in *records* of any length. The name, address and length of each record is "
"held in a directory at the start of the file."
msgstr ""
"Molpro 使用三个顺序文本文件，即 *输入文件*\\ 、\\ *输出文件* 和 *punch 文件*\\ 。punch "
"文件是输出的简短形式，包含最重要的数据和结果，例如几何结构、能量、偶极矩等。punch 文件可以通过独立的程序 *READPUN* "
"处理，该程序通过关键字选择特定结果，并能够以用户提供的格式生成有序表格。此外，最多有 9 个二进制 Molpro 文件可用，每个文件仅通过其编号（1 到"
" 9）被程序识别。默认情况下，它们是临时文件，通常由程序动态分配，但可以使用 ``FILE`` "
"命令将它们连接到永久文件。每个文件都是直接访问的，并且按字寻址（字通常为 64 位），但被组织成任意长度的 *记录*\\ "
"。每个记录的名称、地址和长度保存在文件开头的目录中。"

msgid ""
"File 1 is the *main file*, holding basis set, geometry, and the one and two "
"electron integrals. By default, file 2 is the *dump file* and used to store "
"the wavefunction information, i.e. orbitals, CI coefficients, and density "
"matrices. File 3 is an auxiliary file which can be used in addition to file "
"2 for restart purposes. Often files 1 and 2 (and 3) are declared as "
"permanent files (see ``FILE``) to enable restarts. Storing the wavefunction "
"information on file 2 is useful, since the integral file is overwritten at "
"each new geometry, while the orbitals and CI coefficients of one calculation"
" can be used as a starting guess for the next calculation at a neighbouring "
"geometry. Files 4 to 8 are used as scratch space, e.g., for sorting the "
"integrals, storage of transformed integrals and of the CI vectors. These "
"files should normally not be made permanent."
msgstr ""
"文件 1 是 *主文件*\\ ，保存基组、几何结构以及单电子和双电子积分。默认情况下，文件 2 是 *转储文件*\\ ，用于存储波函数信息，即轨道、CI"
" 系数和密度矩阵。文件 3 是一个辅助文件，除了文件 2 之外，还可用于重启目的。通常将文件 1 和 2（以及 3）声明为永久文件（参见 "
"``FILE``\\ ）以启用重启。将波函数信息存储在文件 2 上是有用的，因为积分文件在每个新几何结构处都会被覆盖，而一个计算的轨道和 CI "
"系数可以用作相邻几何结构处下一个计算的初始猜测。文件 4 到 8 用作暂存空间，例如，用于排序积分、存储变换积分和 CI "
"向量。这些文件通常不应设为永久文件。"

msgid ""
"Note that the file name appearing in molpro input is always converted to "
"lower case on unix machines."
msgstr "请注意，在 Unix 机器上，molpro 输入中出现的文件名总是被转换为小写。"

msgid "Records"
msgstr "记录"

msgid ""
"Record names are positive integers, and are usually referred to in the "
"format *record.file*, e.g., 2100.2 means the record called 2100 on file 2. "
"Note that these names are quite arbitrary, and their numerical values have "
"nothing to do with the order of the records in the file. Record names "
":math:`\\le` 2000 are reserved for standard quantities (e.g. integrals, "
"properties etc.) and you should never use these in an input, unless you know"
" exactly what you are doing. Some important default records to remember are"
msgstr ""
"记录名称为正整数，通常以 *记录.文件* 的格式引用，例如，2100.2 表示文件 2 上名为 2100 "
"的记录。请注意，这些名称是相当任意的，其数值与文件中记录的顺序无关。记录名称 :math:`\\le` 2000 "
"是为标准量（例如积分、性质等）保留的，除非您确切知道自己在做什么，否则绝不应在输入中使用这些名称。一些需要记住的重要默认记录是"

msgid "**2100** RHF dump record (closed and open-shell)"
msgstr "**2100** RHF 转储记录（闭壳层和开壳层）"

msgid "**2200** UHF dump record"
msgstr "**2200** UHF 转储记录"

msgid "**2140** MCSCF dump record"
msgstr "**2140** MCSCF 转储记录"

msgid "**4100** CPHF restart information"
msgstr "**4100** CPHF 重启信息"

msgid "**5000** MCSCF gradient information"
msgstr "**5000** MCSCF 梯度信息"

msgid "**5100** CP-MCSCF gradient information"
msgstr "**5100** CP-MCSCF 梯度信息"

msgid "**5200** MP2 gradient information"
msgstr "**5200** MP2 梯度信息"

msgid "**5300** Hessian restart information"
msgstr "**5300** Hessian 矩阵重启信息"

msgid "**5400** Frequencies restart information"
msgstr "**5400** 频率重启信息"

msgid "**6300** Domain restart information"
msgstr "**6300** 域重启信息"

msgid ""
"If an input contains several wavefunction calculations of the same type, "
"e.g., several MCSCF calculations with different active spaces, the record "
"number will be increased by 1 for each calculation of the same type. Thus, "
"the results of the first SCF calculation in an input are stored in dump "
"record 2100.2, the second SCF in record 2101.2, the first MCSCF in 2140.2, "
"the second MCSCF in 2141.2 and so on. Note that these numbers refer to the "
"occurrence in the input and not on the order in which the calculations are "
"performed in the actual run. If an input or part of it is repeated using "
"``DO`` loops, this ensures that each calculation will start with the "
"orbitals from the corresponding orbitals from the previous cycle, as long as"
" the order of the commands in the input remains unchanged. If for instance "
"the first SCF would be skipped in the second cycle using some ``IF`` / "
"``ENDIF`` structure, the second SCF would still use record 2101.2. Thus, "
"under most circumstances the program defaults are appropriate, and the user "
"does not have to specify the records."
msgstr ""
"如果一个输入包含多个相同类型的波函数计算，例如，多个具有不同活性空间的 MCSCF 计算，则相同类型的每个计算其记录号将增加 1。因此，输入中第一个 "
"SCF 计算的结果存储在转储记录 2100.2 中，第二个 SCF 存储在记录 2101.2 中，第一个 MCSCF 存储在 2140.2 中，第二个 "
"MCSCF 存储在 2141.2 中，依此类推。请注意，这些数字指的是在输入中的出现顺序，而不是计算在实际运行中的执行顺序。如果使用 ``DO`` "
"循环重复输入或其部分内容，只要输入中命令的顺序保持不变，这将确保每个计算都将从上一个循环中对应的轨道开始。例如，如果使用某些 ``IF`` / "
"``ENDIF`` 结构在第二个循环中跳过第一个 SCF，第二个 SCF 仍将使用记录 "
"2101.2。因此，在大多数情况下，程序默认值是合适的，用户无需指定记录。"

msgid ""
"After a restart this logic will still work correctly if the number and "
"sequence of ``SCF`` and ``MCSCF`` commands is kept unchanged. Thus, if you "
"want to skip certain parts of the input after a restart, it is recommended "
"to use ``IF`` / ``ENDIF`` structures or the ``GOTO`` command rather than to "
"delete or comment certain commands. If for some reason this is not possible,"
" the ``START`` and ``ORBITAL`` directives can be used to specify explicitely"
" the records to be used."
msgstr ""
"重启后，如果 ``SCF`` 和 ``MCSCF`` 命令的数量和顺序保持不变，此逻辑仍将正确工作。因此，如果您想在重启后跳过输入的某些部分，建议使用 "
"``IF`` / ``ENDIF`` 结构或 ``GOTO`` 命令，而不是删除或注释某些命令。如果由于某种原因无法做到这一点，可以使用 "
"``START`` 和 ``ORBITAL`` 指令来明确指定要使用的记录。"

msgid ""
"In general we recommend the use of program defaults whenever possible, since"
" this minimizes the probability of input errors and frustration!"
msgstr "通常，我们建议尽可能使用程序默认值，因为这可以最大限度地减少输入错误和挫败感的可能性！"

msgid ""
"After completion of each program step, Molpro prints a summary of the "
"records on each file."
msgstr "每个程序步骤完成后，Molpro 会打印每个文件上记录的摘要。"

msgid "Restart"
msgstr "重启"

msgid ""
"Information from the permanent files is automatically recovered in "
"subsequent calculations. This can be controlled using the ``RESTART`` "
"directive."
msgstr "永久文件中的信息会在后续计算中自动恢复。这可以通过使用 ``RESTART`` 指令来控制。"

msgid "Data set manipulation"
msgstr "数据集操作"

msgid ""
"It is possible to truncate files and rename or copy records using the "
"``DATA`` command. Several standard matrix operations can be performed with "
"``MATROP``, e.g., printing records, linearly combining or multiplying "
"matrices, or forming the trace of a product of two matrices."
msgstr ""
"可以使用 ``DATA`` 命令截断文件以及重命名或复制记录。可以使用 ``MATROP`` "
"执行几种标准的矩阵操作，例如，打印记录、线性组合或相乘矩阵，或计算两个矩阵乘积的迹。"

msgid "Memory allocation"
msgstr "内存分配"

msgid ""
"Molpro can allocate memory dynamically as required by the user. Thus it is "
"not necessary to maintain different versions of the program with different "
"memory sizes. There are two ways to specify the memory: (1) ``MEMORY`` card "
"in Molpro input file; (2) options ``-m`` or ``--memory`` or ``-M`` in the "
"Molpro command line. The latter method is recommended. Please refer to "
"sections `memory specifications "
"<running_molpro_on_parallel_computers.html#memory-specifications>`__ for "
"more details and important information regarding parallel processing."
msgstr ""
"Molpro 可以根据用户需求动态分配内存。因此，无需维护具有不同内存大小的不同版本的程序。有两种指定内存的方法：(1) Molpro 输入文件中的 "
"``MEMORY`` 卡片；(2) Molpro 命令行中的选项 ``-m`` 或 ``--memory`` 或 ``-M``\\ "
"。推荐使用后一种方法。更多详情和关于并行处理的重要信息，请参阅章节 `内存规格 "
"<running_molpro_on_parallel_computers.html#memory-specifications>`__\\ 。"

msgid ""
"If memory is specified using both methods at the same time, ``MEMORY`` card "
"will take precedence. If both ways are omitted, the program will use a "
"default memory size (currently it is :math:`32000000` words, i.e. 256 MB). "
"Please note that: (1) memory specification is in megawords. 1 word is 8 "
"bytes (i.e., the memory size to store one double precision data). (2) memory"
" specification is for each process."
msgstr ""
"如果同时使用两种方法指定内存，\\ ``MEMORY`` 卡片将优先。如果两种方式都省略，程序将使用默认内存大小（当前为 "
":math:`32000000` 字，即 256 MB）。请注意：(1) 内存规格以兆字为单位。1 字为 8 "
"字节（即存储一个双精度数据所需的内存大小）。(2) 内存规格是针对每个进程的。"

msgid "Memory directive in the input file"
msgstr "输入文件中的内存指令"

msgid ""
"By default, all memory specifications are in megawords. The numbers (*m, G, "
"M*) can be appended by a scaling unit, which can be ``K``, ``M``, or ``G`` "
"(case insensitive). If the unit is ``K``, the specification is assumed to be"
" in kilowords (:math:`10^3` words), ``M`` means megawords (:math:`10^6` "
"words), and ``G`` means gigawords (:math:`10^9` words). Blanks or commas "
"have to be inserted between the number and the unit, i.e., 100 m or 100,m "
"are possible specifications of the memory size."
msgstr ""
"默认情况下，所有内存规格均以兆字为单位。数字（\\ *m, G, M*\\ ）可以附加一个缩放单位，可以是 ``K``\\ 、\\ ``M`` 或 "
"``G``\\ （大小写不敏感）。如果单位是 ``K``\\ ，则规格假定为千字（\\ :math:`10^3` 字），\\ ``M`` 表示兆字（\\"
" :math:`10^6` 字），\\ ``G`` 表示吉字（\\ :math:`10^9` 字）。数字和单位之间必须插入空格或逗号，即 100 m 或"
" 100,m 都是有效的内存大小规格。"

msgid "Examples:"
msgstr "示例："

msgid "``MEMORY,90`` requests 90 000 000 words of memory"
msgstr "``MEMORY,90`` 请求 90 000 000 字的内存"

msgid "``MEMORY,500 K`` requests 500 000 words of memory"
msgstr "``MEMORY,500 K`` 请求 500 000 字的内存"

msgid "``MEMORY,2 M`` requests 2 000 000 words of memory"
msgstr "``MEMORY,2 M`` 请求 2 000 000 字的内存"

msgid "``MEMORY,100,M`` requests 100 000 000 words of memory"
msgstr "``MEMORY,100,M`` 请求 100 000 000 字的内存"

msgid "``memory,100 m`` requests 100 000 000 words of memory"
msgstr "``memory,100 m`` 请求 100 000 000 字的内存"

msgid "``MEMORY,1 g`` requests :math:`10^9` words of memory"
msgstr "``MEMORY,1 g`` 请求 :math:`10^9` 字的内存"

msgid ""
"Optionally, the requested GA space or the total allocatable memory (stack "
"memory + GA) can be used. These options have the same meaning and effect as "
"the ``-G`` and ``-M`` command line options, cf. section `memory "
"specifications <running_molpro_on_parallel_computers.html#memory-"
"specifications>`__. ``GA_PREALLOC=0`` or ``GA_PREALLOC=1`` disables or "
"enables GA preallocation, respectively (see sections `GA Installation notes "
"<running_molpro_on_parallel_computers.html#ga-installation-notes>`__ and "
"`memory specifications <running_molpro_on_parallel_computers.html#memory-"
"specifications>`__)."
msgstr ""
"可选地，可以使用请求的 GA 空间或总可分配内存（栈内存 + GA）。这些选项与 ``-G`` 和 ``-M`` "
"命令行选项具有相同的含义和效果，参见章节 `memory specifications "
"<running_molpro_on_parallel_computers.html#memory-specifications>`__\\ 。\\ "
"``GA_PREALLOC=0`` 或 ``GA_PREALLOC=1`` 分别禁用或启用 GA 预分配（参见章节 `GA Installation "
"notes <running_molpro_on_parallel_computers.html#ga-installation-notes>`__ 和"
" `memory specifications <running_molpro_on_parallel_computers.html#memory-"
"specifications>`__\\ ）。"

msgid "Memory option in command line"
msgstr "命令行中的内存选项"

msgid ""
"The ``scale`` (``k``, ``m``, ``g`` and ``K``, ``M``, ``G``) is case "
"sensitive, lower case for decimal and upper case for binary. ``k, m, g`` "
"stand for 1000, 1000 000 and :math:`10^9`; ``K, M, G`` stand for "
":math:`2^{10}`, :math:`2^{20}` and :math:`2^{30}`."
msgstr ""
"``scale``\\ （\\ ``k``\\ 、\\ ``m``\\ 、\\ ``g`` 以及 ``K``\\ 、\\ ``M``\\ 、\\ "
"``G``\\ ）区分大小写，小写表示十进制，大写表示二进制。\\ ``k, m, g`` 代表 1000、1000 000 和 "
":math:`10^9`\\ ；\\ ``K, M, G`` 代表 :math:`2^{10}`\\ 、\\ :math:`2^{20}` 和 "
":math:`2^{30}`\\ 。"

msgid "``-m 1k`` requests 1000 words of memory"
msgstr "``-m 1k`` 请求 1000 字的内存"

msgid "``-m 1K`` requests 1024 words of memory"
msgstr "``-m 1K`` 请求 1024 字的内存"

msgid "``-m 1m`` requests 1000000 words of memory"
msgstr "``-m 1m`` 请求 1000000 字的内存"

msgid "``-m 1M`` requests 1048576 words of memory"
msgstr "``-m 1M`` 请求 1048576 字的内存"

msgid "``-m 1g`` requests :math:`10^9` words of memory"
msgstr "``-m 1g`` 请求 :math:`10^9` 字的内存"

msgid "``-m 1G`` requests :math:`2^{30}` words of memory"
msgstr "``-m 1G`` 请求 :math:`2^{30}` 字的内存"

msgid ""
"For more information please refer to section `memory specifications "
"<running_molpro_on_parallel_computers.html#memory-specifications>`__."
msgstr ""
"更多信息请参阅章节 `内存规格 <running_molpro_on_parallel_computers.html#memory-"
"specifications>`__\\ 。"

msgid "Memory in parallel"
msgstr "并行内存"

msgid ""
"The memory specification is for each process. So the total requested memory "
"in parallel calculation will be the specified memory amount multiplied by "
"the number of compute processes. For example, specifying :math:`100 * 10^6` "
"words for a job with 4 compute processes:"
msgstr ""
"内存规格是针对每个进程的。因此，并行计算中请求的总内存将是指定的内存量乘以计算进程的数量。例如，为一个有 4 个计算进程的作业指定 :math:`100"
" * 10^6` 字："

msgid "``memory,100,m`` in input file"
msgstr "输入文件中的 ``memory,100,m``"

msgid "``-m 100m`` in command line"
msgstr "``-m 100m`` 在命令行中"

msgid ""
"the total requested memory will be :math:`100 * 10^6 * 8 * 4 = 3.2 * 10^9` "
"bytes."
msgstr "请求的总内存将为 :math:`100 * 10^6 * 8 * 4 = 3.2 * 10^9` 字节。"

msgid ""
"In addition, some methods need an significant amount of global array (GA) "
"memory. Please refer to sections `GA Installation notes "
"<running_molpro_on_parallel_computers.html#ga-installation-notes>`__ and "
"`memory specifications <running_molpro_on_parallel_computers.html#memory-"
"specifications>`__ for important information regarding parallel processing."
msgstr ""
"此外，某些方法需要大量的全局数组（GA）内存。关于并行处理的重要信息，请参阅章节 `GA 安装说明 "
"<running_molpro_on_parallel_computers.html#ga-installation-notes>`__ 和 `内存规格"
" <running_molpro_on_parallel_computers.html#memory-specifications>`__\\ 。"

msgid "Multiple passes through the input"
msgstr "多次遍历输入"

msgid ""
"It is possible to perform loops over parts of the input using ``DO`` loops, "
"very much as in ``FORTRAN`` programs. ``DO`` loops may be nested to any "
"reasonable depth. This can be conveniently used, for instance, to compute "
"automatically whole potential energy surfaces."
msgstr ""
"可以使用 ``DO`` 循环对输入的部分内容执行循环，这与 ``FORTRAN`` 程序中的用法非常相似。\\ ``DO`` "
"循环可以嵌套到任何合理的深度。这可以方便地用于，例如，自动计算整个势能面。"

msgid "Symmetry"
msgstr "对称性"

msgid ""
"Molpro can use Abelian point group symmetry only. For molecules with "
"degenerate symmetry, an Abelian subgroup must be used — e.g., :math:`C_{2v}`"
" or :math:`D_{2h}` for linear molecules. The symmetry group which is used is"
" defined in the integral input by combinations of the symmetry elements "
":math:`x`, :math:`y`, and :math:`z`, which specify which coordinate axes "
"change sign under the corresponding generating symmetry operation. It is "
"usually wise to choose :math:`z` to be the unique axis where appropriate "
"(essential for :math:`C_2` and :math:`C_{2h}`). The possibilities in this "
"case are shown in Table `symmetry "
"<general_program_structure.html#symmetry>`__."
msgstr ""
"Molpro 只能使用阿贝尔点群对称性。对于具有简并对称性的分子，必须使用阿贝尔子群——例如，对于线性分子使用 :math:`C_{2v}` 或 "
":math:`D_{2h}`\\ 。所使用的对称群在积分输入中通过对称元素 :math:`x`\\ 、\\ :math:`y` 和 :math:`z` "
"的组合来定义，这些元素指定了在相应的生成对称操作下哪些坐标轴会改变符号。通常明智的做法是在适当的情况下选择 :math:`z` 作为唯一轴（对于 "
":math:`C_2` 和 :math:`C_{2h}` 是必需的）。这种情况下的可能性如表 `对称性 "
"<general_program_structure.html#symmetry>`__ 所示。"

msgid ""
"Normally, Molpro determines the symmetry automatically, and rotates and "
"translates the molecule accordingly. However, explicit symmetry "
"specification is sometimes useful to fix the orientation of the molecule or "
"to use lower symmetries."
msgstr "通常，Molpro 会自动确定对称性，并相应地旋转和平移分子。然而，显式指定对称性有时对于固定分子的方向或使用较低对称性很有用。"

msgid "The symmetry generators for the point groups"
msgstr "点群的对称性生成元"

msgid "Generators"
msgstr "生成元"

msgid "Point group"
msgstr "点群"

msgid "(null card)"
msgstr "(空卡片)"

msgid ":math:`C_1` (i.e. no point group symmetry)"
msgstr ":math:`C_1` (即无点群对称性)"

msgid "``X`` (or ``Y`` or ``Z``)"
msgstr "``X`` (或 ``Y`` 或 ``Z``)"

msgid ":math:`C_s`"
msgstr ":math:`C_s`"

msgid "``XY``"
msgstr "``XY``"

msgid ":math:`C_2`"
msgstr ":math:`C_2`"

msgid "``XYZ``"
msgstr "``XYZ``"

msgid ":math:`C_i`"
msgstr ":math:`C_i`"

msgid "``X,Y``"
msgstr "``X,Y``"

