msgid "Defining the wavefunction (WF)"
msgstr "定义波函数（WF）"

msgid ""
"In all program modules where such information is required, the total "
"symmetry of the :math:`N`-electron wavefunction is defined on ``WF`` "
"(wavefunction) cards in the following way:"
msgstr "在所有需要此类信息的程序模块中，\\ :math:`N` 电子波函数的总对称性通过以下方式在 ``WF``\\ （波函数）卡片上定义："

msgid "or, alternatively"
msgstr "或者，另一种形式"

msgid ""
"This charge will be used in all energy calculations following this input. "
"Note that ``SET`` is required, since ``CHARGE`` is a system variable (cf. "
"section `system variables <variables.html#system-variables>`__)."
msgstr ""
"此电荷将用于此输入之后的所有能量计算。请注意，\\ ``SET`` 是必需的，因为 ``CHARGE`` 是一个系统变量（参见 `系统变量 "
"<variables.html#system-variables>`__ 一节）。"

msgid ""
"If the ``WF`` directive is given outside an command input block, it is "
"treated as global, i.e., the given values are used for all subsequent "
"calculations. Setting the variables ``NELEC``, ``SPIN``, or ``SYMMETRY``, "
"has the same effect giving these on a global ``WF`` directive. If the global"
" ``WF`` directive is given after the variable definition, the values of the "
"variables are replaced by the values given on the ``WF`` directive. Vice "
"versa, if a variable definition follows a global ``WF`` directive, the new "
"value of the variable is used in the following. Note that ``WF`` input cards"
" in command blocks have preference over global ``WF`` directives or input "
"variables."
msgstr ""
"如果 ``WF`` 指令在命令输入块之外给出，它将被视为全局的，即，给定的值将用于所有后续计算。设置变量 ``NELEC``\\ 、\\ "
"``SPIN`` 或 ``SYMMETRY``\\ ，与在全局 ``WF`` 指令上给出这些具有相同的效果。如果在变量定义之后给出全局 ``WF`` "
"指令，则变量的值将被 ``WF`` 指令上给出的值替换。反之，如果变量定义跟在全局 ``WF`` 指令之后，则变量的新值将在后续使用。请注意，命令块中的"
" ``WF`` 输入卡片优先于全局 ``WF`` 指令或输入变量。"

msgid "Defining orbital subspaces (OCC,CLOSED,CORE,FROZEN)"
msgstr "定义轨道子空间 (OCC,CLOSED,CORE,FROZEN)"

msgid ""
"In the SCF, MCSCF, and CI programs it may be necessary to specify how many "
"orbitals in each symmetry are *occupied* (or *internal* in CI), and which of"
" these are *core* or *closed shell* (doubly occupied in all CSFs). This "
"information is provided on the ``OCC``, ``CORE``, and ``CLOSED`` cards in "
"the following way:"
msgstr ""
"在 SCF、MCSCF 和 CI 程序中，可能需要指定每个对称性中有多少轨道是\\ *占据的*\\ （或在 CI 中称为\\ *内部的*\\ "
"），以及其中哪些是\\ *芯轨道*\\ 或\\ *闭壳层*\\ （在所有 CSFs 中双占据）。此信息通过 ``OCC``\\ 、\\ ``CORE``"
" 和 ``CLOSED`` 卡片以下列方式提供："

msgid ""
"``SMALL`` means that all atomic orbitals are correlated for which the cc-"
"pwCVXZ basis are optimized (typically one additional shell of each angular "
"momentum below the valence shell). For :math:`n`\\ d transition metals, the "
":math:`n`\\ s, :math:`(n+1)`\\ s, :math:`n`\\ p, :math:`n`\\ d orbitals are "
"correlated."
msgstr ""
"``SMALL`` 意味着所有 cc-pwCVXZ 基组优化的原子轨道都会被关联（通常是价层以下每个角动量的一个额外壳层）。对于 :math:`n`\\"
" d 过渡金属，\\ :math:`n`\\ s、\\ :math:`(n+1)`\\ s、\\ :math:`n`\\ p、\\ "
":math:`n`\\ d 轨道会被关联。"

msgid ""
"``MIXED`` corresponds to ``SMALL`` but the next lower s and p shells of the "
"p-block elements are not correlated."
msgstr "``MIXED`` 对应于 ``SMALL``\\ ，但 p 区元素的下一个更低的 s 和 p 壳层不被关联。"

msgid ""
"Note that until Molpro 2021.3, the 2s and 2p shells of the second-row "
"elements Al - Ar were correlated with ``MIXED``, but for consistency this "
"has been changed in 2021.4. The old behaviour can be recovered using "
"``MIXED_OLD``."
msgstr ""
"请注意，在 Molpro 2021.3 之前，第二行元素 Al - Ar 的 2s 和 2p 壳层使用 ``MIXED`` "
"时会被关联，但为了保持一致性，这在 2021.4 版本中已更改。可以使用 ``MIXED_OLD`` 恢复旧行为。"

msgid ""
"``LARGE`` means that no inner shells are correlated (default). In transition"
" metals the outermost d-shell and in f-elements the outermost f-shell are "
"treated as valence and always correlated."
msgstr ""
"``LARGE`` 意味着没有内层壳层被关联（默认）。在过渡金属中，最外层的 d 壳层和在 f 区元素中最外层的 f 壳层被视为价层并始终被关联。"

msgid ""
"The most general core definition is possible using the last possibility, "
"where *SYM1, SYM2* etc are atomic symbols and *spdf* are the numbers of core"
" orbitals at the given atom for each angular momentum. For example, for "
"bromine ``CORE,Br=21`` is equivalent to ``CORE,SMALL``, ``CORE,Br=32`` is "
"equivalent to ``CORE,MIXED``, and ``CORE,Br=321`` is equivalent to "
"``CORE,LARGE``. Trailing zeros are optional, i.e. Br=3200, 320, or 32 are "
"equivalent. Atom-specific core specifications cannot exceed the number of "
"large core orbitals for each angular momentum."
msgstr ""
"最通用的芯轨道定义可以使用最后一种可能性，其中 *SYM1, SYM2* 等是原子符号，\\ *spdf* "
"是给定原子上每个角动量的芯轨道数量。例如，对于溴，\\ ``CORE,Br=21`` 等同于 ``CORE,SMALL``\\ ，\\ "
"``CORE,Br=32`` 等同于 ``CORE,MIXED``\\ ，而 ``CORE,Br=321`` 等同于 ``CORE,LARGE``\\ "
"。尾随零是可选的，即 Br=3200、320 或 32 是等效的。特定原子的芯轨道规格不能超过每个角动量的大芯轨道数量。"

msgid ""
"Optionally, SMALL, MIXED, or LARGE can be followed by specifications for "
"individual atoms. In this case these default apply to all atoms that are not"
" explicitly specified."
msgstr "可选地，SMALL、MIXED 或 LARGE 后面可以跟针对单个原子的具体说明。在这种情况下，这些默认设置适用于所有未明确指定的原子。"

