msgid ""
"The program automatically checks if the orbitals with the lowest orbital "
"energies correspond to the requested core orbitals, and if necessary "
"orbitals are swapped as required. Within the set of core orbitals, this "
"check can only be performed if ``SMALL`` or ``MIXED`` is given. If one "
"specifies the absolute number of core orbitals the check is not possible "
"since the program does not know which type the core orbitals should have."
msgstr ""
"程序会自动检查能量最低的轨道是否与请求的芯轨道对应，并在必要时按要求交换轨道。在芯轨道集合内，仅当指定了 ``SMALL`` 或 ``MIXED`` "
"时才能执行此检查。如果指定了芯轨道的绝对数量，则无法进行检查，因为程序不知道芯轨道应为何种类型。"

msgid ""
"Note that the ``OCC`` and ``CLOSED`` cards have slightly different meanings "
"in the SCF, MCSCF and CI or CCSD programs. In SCF and MCSCF, *occupied* "
"orbitals are those which occur in any of the CSFs. In electron correlation "
"methods (CI, MPn, CCSD etc), however, ``OCC`` denotes the orbitals which are"
" occupied in any of the *reference* CSFs. In the MCSCF, ``FROZEN`` orbitals "
"are doubly occupied in all CSFs and *frozen* (not optimized), while  "
"*closed* denotes all doubly occupied orbitals (frozen plus optimized). In "
"the CI and CCSD programs, *core* orbitals are those which are not correlated"
" and *closed* orbitals are those which are doubly occupied in all reference "
"CSFs."
msgstr ""
"请注意，\\ ``OCC`` 和 ``CLOSED`` 卡片在 SCF、MCSCF 以及 CI 或 CCSD 程序中的含义略有不同。在 SCF 和 "
"MCSCF 中，\\ *占据*\\ 轨道是出现在任何组态态函数中的轨道。然而，在电子相关方法（CI、MPn、CCSD 等）中，\\ ``OCC`` "
"表示在任何\\ *参考*\\ 组态态函数中被占据的轨道。在 MCSCF 中，\\ ``FROZEN`` 轨道在所有组态态函数中均为双占据且被\\ "
"*冻结*\\ （不优化），而\\ *闭*\\ 轨道表示所有双占据轨道（冻结的加上优化的）。在 CI 和 CCSD 程序中，\\ *芯*\\ "
"轨道是那些不参与相关的轨道，而\\ *闭*\\ 轨道是在所有参考组态态函数中双占据的轨道。"

msgid ""
"``OCC``, ``CORE`` and ``CLOSED`` directives are generally required in each "
"program module where they are relevant; however, the program remembers the "
"most recently used values, and so the directives may be omitted if the "
"orbital spaces are not to be changed from their previous values. Note that "
"this information is also preserved across restarts. Note also, as with the "
"``WF`` information, sensible defaults are assumed for these orbital spaces. "
"For full details, see the appropriate program description."
msgstr ""
"``OCC``\\ 、\\ ``CORE`` 和 ``CLOSED`` "
"指令通常在每个相关的程序模块中都需要；但是，程序会记住最近使用的值，因此如果轨道空间不打算从其先前值更改，则可以省略这些指令。请注意，此信息在重启时也会保留。另请注意，与"
" ``WF`` 信息一样，这些轨道空间会采用合理的默认值。有关完整详细信息，请参阅相应的程序描述。"

msgid "``OCC,4,2,1,CONTEXT=MULTI``"
msgstr "``OCC,4,2,1,CONTEXT=MULTI``"

msgid ""
"Alternatively, the context can be appended to the directive name with an "
"underscore. For example"
msgstr "或者，可以将上下文以下划线附加到指令名称后。例如"

msgid "``OCC_MULTI,4,2,1``"
msgstr "``OCC_MULTI,4,2,1``"

msgid "is equivalent to the previous form."
msgstr "与前面的形式等价。"

msgid ""
"The occupation and core settings are usually molecule specific and depend on"
" the symmetry and charges. They can also change if dummy atoms are defined. "
"Therefore, global settings should be used with care. In molpro2021.4 or "
"later it is possible to specify global core types "
"(``CORE,SMALL|MIXED|LARGE``); these work also if the molecule or symmetry "
"changes, or if dummy atoms are used. Specifying core orbitals in this way is"
" preferable since the orbitals are appropriately reordered, if necessary "
"(see above). Note that contexts cannot be given if core types are given; "
"also atom-specific core definitions are only possible within command blocks."
msgstr ""
"占据数和芯轨道的设置通常是分子特定的，并依赖于对称性和电荷。如果定义了哑原子，它们也可能改变。因此，应谨慎使用全局设置。在 molpro2021.4 "
"或更高版本中，可以指定全局芯轨道类型（\\ ``CORE,SMALL|MIXED|LARGE``\\ "
"）；这些设置即使在分子或对称性发生变化，或使用哑原子时也有效。以这种方式指定芯轨道是更可取的，因为轨道会在必要时被适当地重新排序（见上文）。请注意，如果指定了芯轨道类型，则不能给出上下文；此外，特定于原子的芯轨道定义只能在命令块内进行。"

msgid ""
"Local input given within command blocks has preference over global input."
msgstr "命令块内给出的局部输入优先于全局输入。"

msgid "Selecting orbitals and density matrices (ORBITAL, DENSITY)"
msgstr "选择轨道和密度矩阵 (ORBITAL, DENSITY)"

msgid ""
"[sec:orbitals] As outlined in section `records "
"<general_program_structure.html#records>`__, the information for each SCF or"
" MCSCF calculation is stored in a *dump record*. Dump records contain "
"orbitals, density matrices, orbital energies, occupation numbers, fock "
"matrices and other information as wavefunction symmetries etc. Subsequent "
"calculation can access the orbitals and density matrices from a particular "
"record using the ``ORBITAL`` and ``DENSITY`` directives, respectively. These"
" input cards have the same structure in all programs. The general format of "
"the ``ORBITAL`` and ``DENSITY`` directives is as follows:"
msgstr ""
"[sec:orbitals] 如 `records <general_program_structure.html#records>`__ "
"一节所述，每次 SCF 或 MCSCF 计算的信息都存储在一个\\ *转储记录*\\ 中。转储记录包含轨道、密度矩阵、轨道能量、占据数、Fock "
"矩阵以及波函数对称性等其他信息。后续计算可以分别使用 ``ORBITAL`` 和 ``DENSITY`` "
"指令从特定记录中访问轨道和密度矩阵。这些输入卡片在所有程序中具有相同的结构。\\ ``ORBITAL`` 和 ``DENSITY`` "
"指令的一般格式如下："

msgid ""
"If ``OVL`` is specified, the starting orbitals are obtained by maximizing "
"the overlap with previous orbitals. By default, this is used if the basis "
"dimension of the previous orbitals is different then the current one. If "
"``OVL`` is specified this procedure is used even if the basis dimensions are"
" the same, which is occasionally useful if the contraction scheme changed."
msgstr ""
"如果指定了 ``OVL``\\ ，则通过最大化与先前轨道的重叠来获得起始轨道。默认情况下，当先前轨道的基组维度与当前不同时使用此方法。如果指定了 "
"``OVL``\\ ，即使基组维度相同也会使用此过程，这在收缩方案改变时偶尔有用。"

msgid ""
"If ``IGNORE_ERROR`` is specified, MPn or triples calculations can be forced "
"with other than canonical orbitals. Note that this can lead to meaningless "
"results! Note that in MULTI ``IGNORE_ERROR`` must be given on the ``START`` "
"directive, since in this program ``ORBITAL`` is used to define the new "
"orbitals."
msgstr ""
"如果指定了 ``IGNORE_ERROR``\\ ，则可以强制使用非正则轨道进行 MPn 或三重激发计算。请注意，这可能导致无意义的结果！注意，在 "
"MULTI 中，\\ ``IGNORE_ERROR`` 必须在 ``START`` 指令中给出，因为在该程序中 ``ORBITAL`` 用于定义新轨道。"

msgid ""
"If any of the above options are given, they must be obeyed strictly, i.e., "
"the program aborts if the request cannot be fulfilled."
msgstr "如果指定了上述任一选项，则必须严格遵守，即如果请求无法满足，程序将中止。"

msgid "Plugins"
msgstr "插件"

msgid ""
"Molpro can host suitably prepared external programs as “plugins”. They are "
"launched using MPI’s spawn mechanism, and therefore the user must take care "
"of any job-scheduling constraints on the number and placement of MPI "
"processes. The following syntax in the input file will cause the plugin to "
"be launched."
msgstr ""
"Molpro 可以托管经过适当准备的外部程序作为“插件”。它们使用 MPI 的派生机制启动，因此用户必须注意作业调度对 MPI "
"进程数量和位置的任何限制。输入文件中的以下语法将导致插件被启动。"

msgid ""
"*command* is the name of the executable of the plugin. It can be given as an"
" absolute path name, or a relative path. If it is a simple name (no ``/`` "
"characters), it will be searched for in the same directory as Molpro’s "
"executable, and this will be the normal mode of use. If the plugin is not "
"found, and *command* does not have a filename suffix, then the suffix "
"``.exe`` will be assumed."
